      "text": [
        {
          "_key": "92f257082672",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "38db4f8a0416",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "em",
                "strong",
                "6092f37777f5"
              ],
              "text": "Le droit d'aînesse"
            },
            {
              "_key": "5993cbe86b83",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " is an "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00223e5103ec",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "em",
                "cce9f192a465"
              ],
              "text": "opéra bouffe"
            },
            {
              "_key": "375e50d32e81",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " composed by "
            },
            {
              "_key": "1feea7162434",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "1c5db6924d9f"
              ],
              "text": "Francis Chassaigne"
            },
            {
              "_key": "d8355127bd8a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". The original French "
            },
            {
              "_key": "f733e96539fa",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "0e970f8be918"
              ],
              "text": "libretto"
            },
            {
              "_key": "426252ad92a3",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " was written by "
            },
            {
              "_key": "cc925690adf0",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "249cc8115605"
              ],
              "text": "Eugène Leterrier"
            },
            {
              "_key": "598820d4701c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "68d6dffb5b79",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "1914f753ebfd"
              ],
              "text": "Albert Vanloo"
            },
            {
              "_key": "d853090d21e6",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", with an English-language version titled "
            },
            {
              "_key": "5a1919fda592",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "em"
              ],
              "text": "Falka"
            },
            {
              "_key": "d791b621655b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " translated and adapted by "
            },
            {
              "_key": "6db8072215b1",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "939c2a752ddd"
              ],
              "text": "Henry Brougham Farnie"
            },
            {
              "_key": "a9b2b48d13f8",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". The story concerns an arranged marriage intended to make a governor's heir, his nephew, an aristocrat. Through a series of mishaps that place the governor's nephew and his niece each in danger, the niece, Falka, becomes the noble heir. "
            },
            {
              "_key": "493fabc94682",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "em"
              ],
              "text": "Falka"
            },
            {
              "_key": "7c429a79e5ab",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " was first produced at the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "4f3a380589a2",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "c54bb73a04a6"
              ],
              "text": "Comedy Theatre"
            },
            {
              "_key": "bddbdcfe2d38",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " in London on 29 October 1883, the same year as the French premiere, with "
            },
            {
              "_key": "4effeb7d8f74",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "caffe6eee943"
              ],
              "text": "Violet Cameron"
            },
            {
              "_key": "4beb11414406",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " in the title role of Falka, running for 157 performances. It was revived at the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "69f7ac4b38a4",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "250aca325af3"
              ],
              "text": "Avenue Theatre"
            },
            {
              "_key": "913703baab6b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " in 1885, still starring Cameron, and also enjoyed successful productions in Australia, New Zealand and the United States, including productions in 1884 and 1900 on "
            },
            {
              "_key": "06ab20a5a3f3",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "7b3b8de620aa"
              ],
              "text": "Broadway"
            },
            {
              "_key": "6c6a2ce6cda8",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ". This poster for "
            },
            {
              "_key": "95ff96843ec8",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "em"
              ],
              "text": "Falka"
            },
            {
              "_key": "82ee49178605",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " was produced for a production at the "
            },
            {
              "_key": "8133d0ee552e",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "777695428ea7"
              ],
              "text": "Royal Lyceum Theatre"
            },
            {
              "_key": "5ab0215b04d7",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", Edinburgh, in 1885."
            }
          ],
